The City reported, among others, the following significant accomplishments in CY 2022:
a. Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19) Response:
Continued mass vaccination at various vaccination centers within the City;
Purchased 20,000 additional tablets for Molnupiravir for Mild COVID-19 Patients
Purchased 2,500 boxes of Bexovid, a COVID-19 medicinal drug to mild to moderate cases; and
Purchased 30,000 doses of Pfizer vaccines for 5-11 years.
b. Opening of New Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Medicine Center at Sta. Ana Hospital;
c. Conducted the Nilad Tree-Planting Activity at Manila Zoo and Intramuros;
d. Granted P100,000.00 cash gift for three centenarians;
e. Kalinga sa Manila Project to six districts of Manila;
f. Distribution of monetary assistance to families affected by multiple fire incidents;
g. Distribution of Christmas food boxes to six districts of Manila;
h. Construction/repair/rehabilitation/improvement/upgrading/installation of various structures and facilities:
Completion of the following major infrastructure projects:
1. Redevelopment of the Manila Zoo;
2. Construction of Tondominium 1 and 2;
3. Construction of Binondominium 2;
4. Construction of 10-storey Bagong Ospital ng Maynila and Parking Building;
5. Construction of four-storey, 24 classrooms building at A. Maceda High School;
6. Construction of four-storey RC Building I at Bg. Barangay Elementary School;
7. Installations of Solar Studs (Phase 2);
8. Arroceros Urban Forest Park Redevelopment; and
9. Construction of three-storey Community Hospital at BASECO Compound.
Ongoing construction of the following projects:
1. Installation of traffic signal lanterns at various street intersections in the City;
2. Construction of Dr. Albert Elementary School;
3. Construction of Rosauro Almario Elementary School;
4. Construction of Manila Science High School;
5. Construction of San Sebastian Residences;
6. Construction of Pedro Gil Residences;
7. Construction of San Lazaro Residences;
8. Sewerage Plant (Waste Water Treatment Plant);
9. Construction of the Administrative Building at Manila Boystown Complex;
10. Construction of 10-storey, 232 classrooms school building at Ramon Magsaysay High School; and
11. Installation of solar road studs (Phase 3).
In the same year, the City received the following awards/recognitions:
CY 2022 Digital Governance Awards:
1. Government Internal Operations (G2G) Award - City Level
2. 1st Place: Digital Cold Chain Principle: Dickson-One Software) Ensuring Vaccine Safety: The City of Manila/Sta. Ana Hospital Response
3. Business Empowerment (G2B) Award - City Level
4. 2nd Place: Go! BPLS
CY 2022 Seal of Good Financial Housekeeping
Excellence in Digital Public Service awarded by GCash in the Digital Excellence Awards
17th Association of Tourism Officers in the Philippines Pearl Awards
1. 1st runner up for Best Tourism Month/Week Celebration (City Level) and for Best Program for Culture and Arts (City Level)
2. 2nd runner up for Best Tourism Promotion - Publication (City Level)
3. Best Tourism Promotion Video (City Level)
